
This turned out WAY better than it should have. It was a total quick and dirty sauce built around the weird sausages I found in the store and a jar of premade marinara sauce.

Sauce :

Start frying 1 pack of Arsernio’s chicken spinach & feta sausages. In olive oil
When the sausages are getting a bit brown on both sides add..
1 1/2 slivered onions.
1 deseeded and diced paseo pepper.
2 deseeded and diced (fine) jalapeño peppers.
A little bit of red pepper flakes. Not a lot.
Get these frying, salt & pepper to taste.

When all of the onions are beginning to get clear, add 1 box of sliced mushrooms.
Fry all this up, adding salt, pepper & oil as necessary. Along with dribbling in water now and then to deglaze the pan. Do this ’till the onions, peppers & mushrooms look done.
Add in one bowl of crushed garlic. Let it “bloom”. (Fry for about a minute.)
Add in one jar of.. RAO’S Homemade Tomato Basil sauce. - It’s what Ma bought. Tasted great.

The final adjustment is to add pinches of sugar to balance out the taste.

Noodles :
Get a pot of salted water boiling. 
Add Some olive oil.
Add a medium to large shake of dried oregano.
Add the remains of the crushed garlic from the sauce. (Not all gets through the crusher)

That's it. Serve with parmesan cheese. Really tasty!


